Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2
https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/
W3C Recommendation. Copyright World Wide Web Consortium.

The contrast ratio formula and the 4.5:1 text threshold (1.4.3), the target size
minimum and its spacing exception (2.5.8), visible focus (2.4.7), reflow without
horizontal scrolling (1.4.10) and motion from interactions (2.3.3) are WCAG's. The
checks implement them; no WCAG text is reproduced.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Web Interface Guidelines, Vercel Labs
https://github.com/vercel-labs/web-interface-guidelines
MIT License. Copyright (c) 2025 Vercel Labs.

These checks enforce rules taken from the guidelines: no `transition: all`,
`touch-action: manipulation` on controls, `autocomplete="off"` and
`spellcheck="false"` on search inputs, a `theme-color` meta that matches the page,
and tabular figures in number columns. The hand-review checklist in the plugin's
reference folder is a paraphrase of the guidelines, sorted by what the checks cover.
